            <div xml:id="d533">

                <pb facs="0562" n="454" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.841 Surtax/36: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-08-26T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 26,
                                1927—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Department has been shown cable of August 23 from Shanghai office U. S. Steel
                    Products Company reading in part “Have cleared S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Mobile City</hi> without payment illegal 25 per cent surtax tonnage dues on
                    the advice American Consul.”</p>
                <p>Department’s telegram to you of August 17, 3 p.m., did not instruct you to advise
                    steamship owners not to pay tonnage surtax. Question should be left to decision
                    of Steamship Company at whose risk clearance is given.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Castle</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
